From f594988aaa0e89f0f9f22b5d6b982d788e885653
Subject: Download the ffmpeg/BoringSSL-prefixed libwebrtc prebuilts
Origin: https://github.com/robtfm/client-sdk-rust/commit/f594988aaa0e89f0f9f22b5d6b982d788e885653
Date: 2026-10-25T00:53:05+01:00

Upstream's webrtc-a545de4 prebuilts for macOS and Windows ship Chromium's
ffmpeg and BoringSSL with unprefixed symbols (the LK_ prefixing added in
livekit/rust-sdks#1534 is applied by build_linux.sh only). Linked
statically into an executable that also links its own ffmpeg, those
definitions win: ffmpeg loses its network protocols ("Protocol not found"
on https sources) and decoders. The Linux archives also leave 229
BoringSSL exports unprefixed.

The webrtc-a545de4-prefixed release re-hosts upstream's six desktop
archives unchanged except that the ffmpeg and BoringSSL symbol families
are renamed with llvm-objcopy (webrtc_ prefix, remap-webrtc.sh attached
to the release). WEBRTC_TAG changes too so the download cache directory
does not alias the stock archive.

(cherry picked from commit 1aff3eb093597161137078d0d094d073772e03f6)
---
diff --git a/webrtc-sys/build/src/lib.rs b/webrtc-sys/build/src/lib.rs
index 4dc7d89a2a71959726eb0bf40af16045a8552878..473f78f16125e1f1e1c2b50ee2c857ae1b5e9729 100644
--- a/webrtc-sys/build/src/lib.rs
+++ b/webrtc-sys/build/src/lib.rs
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@ use regex::Regex;
 use reqwest::StatusCode;
 
 pub const SCRATH_PATH: &str = "livekit_webrtc";
-pub const WEBRTC_TAG: &str = "webrtc-a545de4";
+pub const WEBRTC_TAG: &str = "webrtc-a545de4-prefixed";
 pub const IGNORE_DEFINES: [&str; 2] = ["CR_CLANG_REVISION", "CR_XCODE_VERSION"];
 
 pub fn target_os() -> String {
@@ -100,7 +100,7 @@ pub fn prebuilt_dir() -> path::PathBuf {
 
 pub fn download_url() -> String {
     format!(
-        "https://github.com/livekit/rust-sdks/releases/download/{}/{}.zip",
+        "https://github.com/robtfm/client-sdk-rust/releases/download/{}/{}.zip",
         WEBRTC_TAG,
         format!("webrtc-{}", webrtc_triple())
     )
